==Vocabulary==

===Crop plants===
Below are some crop plants that have been found in the Southern Neolithic complex of [[Karnataka]] and [[Andhra Pradesh]], along with their Proto-Dravidian or Proto-South Dravidian reconstructions by {{harvp|Southworth|2005}}. In some cases, the proto-form glosses differ from the species identified from archaeological sites. For example, the two Southern Neolithic staple grasses ''[[Brachiaria]] ramosa'' and ''[[Setaria verticillata]]'' respectively correspond to the reconstructed Proto-Dravidian forms for ''[[Sorghum vulgare]]'' and ''[[Setaria italica]]'' as early Dravidian speakers shifted to [[millet]] species that were later introduced to South India.{{sfn|Southworth|2005}}

